      "general": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "altText": {
              "expr": {
                "Literal": {
                  "Value": "'Table of schools and year groups showing distinct students and the present, known and expected student-days that build the rate and coverage, then the marked work score, how much of the work is marked, and how many learners stand behind that score. Attendance follows the period you selected; marked work covers the whole reporting period, because the only date on a piece of set work is the class due date. The marked work columns follow the Subject slicer and the attendance columns do not, since attendance carries no section. With more than one subject selected the marked work score combines marking schemes, so read it down the column as a comparison between schools only when a single subject is chosen.'"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
